<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | IRMARO"
  description="Privacy Policy for irmaro.com, including information about personal data processing, the contact form, service providers, cookies and data subject rights."
  lang="en"
  pageKey="privacy"
>
  <LegalDocument
    lang="en"
    eyebrow="PRIVACY"
    title="Privacy Policy"
    lastUpdated="27 August 2026"
  >
    <p class="legal-intro">This Privacy Policy explains how I process the personal data of people who use www.irmaro.com (the “Website”) or contact me in connection with the coaching and mentoring services I offer.</p>

    <p class="legal-intro">I take the privacy of Website users seriously and process personal data in accordance with applicable law, in particular Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (the General Data Protection Regulation, “GDPR”) and applicable Finnish law.</p>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
      <p>The controller of your personal data is:</p>
      <div class="legal-details">
        <p><strong>Irma Rosenvik / Irmaro</strong></p>
        <p>Hiidentie 4 F 6, 90550 Oulu</p>
        <p>Business ID FI36472034 / Y-tunnus 3647203-4</p>
        <p>Email: <a href="mailto:irma.rosenvik@gmail.com">irma.rosenvik@gmail.com</a></p>
      </div>
      <p>If you have any questions about how your personal data is processed, you can contact me at the email address above.</p>
      <p>No Data Protection Officer (DPO) has been appointed because the nature and scale of the business do not require one.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>2. Personal data I may process</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you use the Website and how you contact me, I may process:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your first name or full name;</li>
        <li>your email address;</li>
        <li>information included in a message sent through the contact form;</li>
        <li>information relating to an enquiry about coaching, mentoring or another service I offer;</li>
        <li>information you voluntarily provide when arranging or taking part in a Session.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>If you voluntarily provide additional information during our contact or a Session, I may also process that information where necessary to respond to your enquiry or provide the requested Service.</p>
      <p>Please do not use the contact form to send information that is not necessary for your enquiry, particularly sensitive information or special categories of personal data.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>3. Why I process personal data</h2>
      <p>I may process personal data for the following purposes:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>to respond to an enquiry sent through the contact form or by email;</li>
        <li>to communicate with someone interested in coaching or mentoring services;</li>
        <li>to arrange, organise and deliver coaching or mentoring Sessions;</li>
        <li>to provide requested services such as career coaching, CV review, cover letter review or LinkedIn profile review;</li>
        <li>to maintain documentation that is necessary in connection with the Services;</li>
        <li>to comply with legal obligations, particularly tax and accounting obligations where applicable;</li>
        <li>to establish, exercise or defend legal claims;</li>
        <li>to protect the Website and prevent misuse.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>I will not use personal data for purposes other than those described above without informing the person concerned and, where required, establishing an appropriate legal basis.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>4. Legal bases for processing</h2>
      <p>Depending on the circumstances, personal data is processed on one or more of the legal bases set out in Article 6 GDPR, in particular:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Article 6(1)(b) GDPR</strong> – where processing is necessary to take steps at your request before entering into a contract or to perform a contract, for example when arranging and delivering a Session;</li>
        <li><strong>Article 6(1)(c) GDPR</strong> – where processing is necessary to comply with a legal obligation to which the controller is subject;</li>
        <li><strong>Article 6(1)(f) GDPR</strong> – where processing is necessary for my legitimate interests, such as communicating with people interested in my Services, maintaining Website security, or establishing, exercising or defending legal claims;</li>
        <li><strong>Article 6(1)(a) GDPR</strong> – where processing is based on consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Where processing is based on consent, you can withdraw your consent at any time. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before consent was withdrawn.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>5. Do you have to provide your data?</h2>
      <p>Providing personal data through the contact form is voluntary. However, information needed to respond to your enquiry must be provided if you would like me to contact you.</p>
      <p>If you do not provide information necessary to handle your enquiry or provide a Service, I may be unable to respond or deliver that Service.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>6. Recipients of personal data</h2>
      <p>Personal data may be shared with service providers that support my business and process data on my behalf, including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Netlify, Inc.</strong> – Website hosting and technical infrastructure;</li>
        <li><strong>Netlify, Inc.</strong> – technical operation of the contact form (Netlify Forms), including security and anti-spam functionality;</li>
        <li><strong>Google</strong> – Gmail email services used for correspondence;</li>
        <li>providers of online meeting tools where they are used, including Google Meet and Microsoft Teams;</li>
        <li>accounting or legal service providers where necessary;</li>
        <li>providers of other IT tools where their involvement is necessary to operate the business or provide Services.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Personal data may also be disclosed to public authorities or other authorised bodies where disclosure is required by law.</p>
      <p>I use service providers only where their involvement is appropriate and necessary for the operation of my business, and I take appropriate steps to ensure lawful processing of personal data.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>7. Transfers outside the European Economic Area</h2>
      <p>Some services I use may be provided by organisations established outside the European Economic Area (EEA), or may involve transfers of personal data outside the EEA.</p>
      <p>Where such a transfer takes place, it will be carried out in accordance with the GDPR, for example on the basis of a European Commission adequacy decision or using appropriate safeguards such as Standard Contractual Clauses where required.</p>
      <p>As at the date of this Privacy Policy, this is particularly relevant to Netlify (Website hosting and contact form services) and Google (Gmail). These providers may use infrastructure or subprocessors outside the EEA, including in the United States. Where the use of a particular service involves an international transfer, the transfer will rely on an appropriate mechanism under Chapter V GDPR, such as an adequacy decision, the EU–US Data Privacy Framework where applicable to the recipient, or Standard Contractual Clauses together with any additional safeguards required in the circumstances.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>8. How long I keep personal data</h2>
      <p>I keep personal data only for as long as necessary for the purpose for which it was collected.</p>
      <p>In particular:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>information submitted through the contact form will be retained for as long as necessary to handle the enquiry and any related contact, followed by a period appropriate to the nature of the matter;</li>
        <li>information connected with the provision of a Service will be retained for the period necessary to provide that Service and for any further period required by law or necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal claims;</li>
        <li>information that must be retained for tax, accounting or other legal purposes will be kept for the period required by the relevant law;</li>
        <li>information processed on the basis of consent will be kept until consent is withdrawn unless continued retention is justified by another legal basis.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>After the relevant retention period has expired, personal data will be deleted or anonymised unless continued storage is required or permitted by law.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>9. Your data protection rights</h2>
      <p>Subject to the conditions set out in the GDPR, you may have the following rights in relation to your personal data:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>the right of access;</li>
        <li>the right to obtain a copy of your data;</li>
        <li>the right to have inaccurate or incomplete data corrected;</li>
        <li>the right to erasure (“the right to be forgotten”) where the GDPR conditions are met;</li>
        <li>the right to restriction of processing;</li>
        <li>the right to data portability where applicable;</li>
        <li>the right to object to processing based on legitimate interests;</li>
        <li>the right to withdraw consent at any time where processing is based on consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise your rights, please contact me at <a href="mailto:Irma.rosenvik@gmail.com">Irma.rosenvik@gmail.com</a>.</p>
      <p>I will respond to requests relating to data subject rights without undue delay and no later than within the period required by the GDPR.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>10. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
      <p>If you believe that your personal data is being processed in breach of applicable data protection law, you have the right to lodge a complaint with the competent supervisory authority.</p>
      <p>Where the competent Finnish authority applies, this is the Office of the Data Protection Ombudsman (Tietosuojavaltuutetun toimisto).</p>
      <p>You are also welcome to contact me first so that I have an opportunity to explain the situation and address the issue.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>11. Contact form</h2>
      <p>If you use the contact form on the Website, I process the information you provide in order to handle your enquiry and contact you. The form is technically operated using Netlify Forms. A submission may be stored in Netlify’s infrastructure and, according to Netlify’s documentation, form submissions are automatically screened for spam using Akismet.</p>
      <p>As a rule, the form asks for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>your name;</li>
        <li>your email address;</li>
        <li>the content of your message or other information needed to handle the enquiry.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>I do not use information submitted through the contact form to send unsolicited marketing communications unless I have an appropriate legal basis for doing so.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>12. Arranging a Session</h2>
      <p>As at the date of this Privacy Policy, the Website does not allow users to book appointments independently or make online payments. The contact form is used only to send an enquiry. Once I receive it, I may contact you by email or by phone, if you have provided a telephone number, to agree a date, the scope of the Service and the next steps in our cooperation. If an external booking system is introduced in the future, this Privacy Policy will be updated before that system is put into use.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>13. Online Sessions</h2>
      <p>Where coaching or mentoring Sessions take place online, external online communication platforms may be used.</p>
      <p>In that case, participant data may be processed by the operator of the chosen platform in accordance with its own privacy policy.</p>
      <p>As at the date of this Privacy Policy, the Website is not integrated with one permanent video-conferencing platform. If a Session is to take place online, the specific tool to be used — for example Zoom, Google Meet, Microsoft Teams or another agreed service — will be confirmed before the meeting. The operator of the selected platform may process information necessary to establish and secure the connection, including identification and technical data, in accordance with its own terms and privacy policy. I limit the information shared to what is necessary to conduct the Session.</p>
      <p>Sessions are not recorded unless you are clearly informed in advance and an appropriate legal basis has been established, including your consent where consent is required.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>14. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
      <p>The Website may use cookies and similar technologies.</p>
      <p>Cookies may be used, in particular, to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>ensure that the Website functions correctly;</li>
        <li>remember user settings;</li>
        <li>maintain security;</li>
        <li>analyse use of the Website;</li>
        <li>support statistical or marketing activities where such tools are used.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Cookies that are necessary for the Website to function may be used without consent where permitted by applicable law. Where consent is required for a cookie, it will be obtained through an appropriate consent mechanism.</p>
      <p>As at the date of this Privacy Policy, the Website does not use Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, remarketing tools or other tools for advertising profiling. The Website may use only cookies or similar technologies that are necessary for its proper operation, security, or to provide functionality expressly requested by the user, where those technologies are used by the underlying infrastructure. The hosting provider may also process technical connection logs such as IP address, browser type, date and time of the request, and security-related information where necessary to provide and secure the service. The Website currently has no integrated booking or online payment system. If Cal.com, Stripe or other tools using cookies or similar technologies are introduced in the future, this Privacy Policy and, where required, the consent mechanism will be updated before those tools are launched.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>15. Data security</h2>
      <p>I take appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect personal data against unauthorised access, loss, destruction, alteration or disclosure.</p>
      <p>The safeguards used are appropriate to the nature, scope and risk of the processing.</p>
      <p>However, no method of transmitting data over the Internet and no method of electronic storage can guarantee absolute security.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>16. Automated decision-making and profiling</h2>
      <p>Personal data relating to Website users is not used for decisions based solely on automated processing, including profiling, that produce legal effects or similarly significantly affect the person concerned.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>17. Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time, particularly where there are changes to the way the Website operates, the services used or applicable law.</p>
      <p>The current version of the Privacy Policy will be published on the Website together with the date of the latest update.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section-block">
      <h2>18. Contact</h2>
      <p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or how your personal data is processed, please contact me:</p>
      <div class="legal-details">
        <p><strong>Irma Rosenvik / Irmaro</strong></p>
        <p>Email: <a href="mailto:irma.rosenvik@gmail.com">irma.rosenvik@gmail.com</a></p>
        <p>Website: www.irmaro.com</p>
      </div>
      <p>Last updated: 27 August 2026</p>
    </section>
  </LegalDocument>
</BaseLayout>
